  recipeId: thermal
  concept: 'Authored objective: Prove protection and complete a fresh reboot.

    Authored
    requirement: Open the fan under load, verify shutdown, isolate and restore cooling,
    reset explicitly and requalify.

    General teaching principle: Thermal control
    depends on measured temperatures, loads, feedback and operating limits over time.

    Only
    fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A thermostat illustrates the need to distinguish a measured condition
    from a chosen setpoint.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A fan command by itself does not prove that thermal protection is
    effective.
